From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Bienvenu <davidbienvenu@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:42:26 -0700
Subject: [a11y] Guard against re-entrancy during Windows accessibility updates

Synchronous accessibility event dispatch on Windows can re-enter
browser and accessibility code before returning. Hold references to
platform COM objects and check manager, node, and frame host liveness
across synchronous event notifications and parent tree updates.

AX-Relnotes: n/a.
Bug: 574378401
Change-Id: Iab79194341253361eae47066413e25049e777227
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8595191
Reviewed-by: Greg Thompson <grt@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Nasko Oskov <nasko@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: David Bienvenu <davidbienvenu@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1726393}

